{"name":"Tufted Leather","hex":"#b96c46","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tufted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having tufts."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of tuft"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tufted"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tufting","blocks":[{"text":"Tufting is a type of textile manufacturing in which a thread is inserted on a primary base.\nIt is an ancient technique for making warm garments, especially mittens. After the knitting is done, short U-shaped loops of extra yarn are introduced through the fabric from the outside so that their ends point inwards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Tufting_gun_%28TD-01%29.jpg/330px-Tufting_gun_%28TD-01%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tufting","wikidata":"Q1644445"},{"title":"Leather","blocks":[{"text":"Leather is a strong, flexible and durable material obtained from the tanning, or chemical treatment, of animal skins and hides to prevent decay. The most common leathers come from cattle, sheep, goats, equine animals, buffalo, pigs and hogs, ostriches, and aquatic animals such as seals and alligators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Leathertools.jpg/330px-Leathertools.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leather","wikidata":"Q286"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Tufting_cloth_stretched_on_frame.jpg/500px-Tufting_cloth_stretched_on_frame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Tufting_cloth_stretched_on_frame.jpg/1280px-Tufting_cloth_stretched_on_frame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Tufting_cloth_stretched_on_frame.jpg/500px-Tufting_cloth_stretched_on_frame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tufting cloth stretched on frame","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATufting_cloth_stretched_on_frame.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Worsted_rug_yarn_on_cones.jpg/500px-Worsted_rug_yarn_on_cones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Worsted_rug_yarn_on_cones.jpg/1280px-Worsted_rug_yarn_on_cones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Worsted_rug_yarn_on_cones.jpg/500px-Worsted_rug_yarn_on_cones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Worsted rug yarn on cones","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWorsted_rug_yarn_on_cones.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Tool%2C_rug-hooking_%28AM_1932.212-1%29.jpg/500px-Tool%2C_rug-hooking_%28AM_1932.212-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Tool%2C_rug-hooking_%28AM_1932.212-1%29.jpg/1280px-Tool%2C_rug-hooking_%28AM_1932.212-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_